join Neeko right
Neeko: And here I thought we were the only ones brave enough to loot Sykul Tower.
leave --All--
join Ada (determined_right) right
Ada: Stupid enough. You mean stupid enough.
leave --All--
join Neeko right
Neeko: Tsk. Whatever. Bravery is just a well-respected form of stupidity.
Neeko: Hey, kid! Are you good?
leave --All--
join Ada right
Ada: Hey, what were you doing down there?
leave --All--
join Player left
update Player (worried)
- Player: I don't... know?
	leave --All--
	join Neeko right
	Neeko: What do you mean you “don’t know”?
	leave --All--
	join Player left
	Player: I walked out of some sort of tube… thing.
	leave --All--
	join Ada right
	Ada: An elevator?
	leave --All--
	join Player left
	Player: No, no–
	leave --All--
	join Neeko right
	Neeko: A subway car?
	leave --All--
	join Player left
	Player: We’re not in england. Wait. Are we?
	leave --All--
	join Ada right
	Ada: Whatever. The real question is what you got.
	leave --All--
	join Player left
	Player: What I... got?
- Player: Uhh... not tax fraud?
	leave --All--
	join Ada right
	Ada: That... hm.
	leave --All--
	join Neeko right
	Neeko: Ada, they looked to the right. As a private eye who has studied psychology, that means... they’re lying. (or was it the left?)
	leave --All--
	join Ada right
	Ada: Yeah, something gives me that impression, too, Sherlock.
	leave --All--
	join Player left
	Player: If it helps, I also wasn’t committing vandalism or destruction of property.
	leave --All--
	join Ada right
	Ada: Wait, what are taxes– nevermind. What I really want to know is what you found down there.
	leave --All--
	join Player left
	Player: I’m sorry... what I found?
leave --All--
join Ada right
Ada: Yeah, you went in there to get stuff, right?
leave --All--
join Neeko right
Neeko: So it’s only logical that you’d bring something back out.
leave --All--
join Ada right
Ada: Psst! Commence maneuver Battery Resuscitation!
[signal arg="start_fight"]
